\begin{abstract}


  We prove that polynomial calculus (and hence also Nullstellensatz) over any field requires linear degree to refute that sparse random regular graphs, as well as sparse \erdosrenyi random graphs, are $3$-colourable. Using the known relation between size and degree
  for polynomial calculus proofs,
  this implies
  strongly exponential lower bounds on proof size.
\end{abstract}






