\noindent The K-S objective function values obtained by 10 repeated calibrations are compared to verify the performance of NCS, TuRBO, and ABC. First, smaller average of the 10 K-S values indicates stronger capability on estimating multi-modal parameters of the algorithm. Secondly, according to the common stochastic optimization algorithm test standard, the Wilcoxon Rank-Sum Test proves whether the performance differences are statistically significant.

