Gaussians can represent both surfaces and volumes alike. Unlike traditional rendering pipelines which treat volumes as scalar fields and surfaces as polygonal meshes, often requiring distinct data structures, Gaussian-based approach allows both types of structures to be encoded similarly. We still require separate shaders when doing photorealistic rendering, but for SciVis use cases having a unified hybrid renderer could support some datasets. See figure \ref{fig:comb-surf-vol}.

