%\subsubsection{Evaluate Antibody Variants}
We evaluated the generated antibody variants from two perspectives: sequence plausibility and binding potential. Sequence plausibility was assessed using the log-likelihood from \texttt{AntiBERTy} \cite{ruffolo2021deciphering}, reflecting how closely mutations align with natural antibody evolution. We also computed inverse folding likelihoods using \texttt{ProteinMPNN} to determine whether each sequence is compatible with its backbone structure—higher scores indicate greater foldability. 
Binding potential was evaluated using three structure-based metrics: (1) binding free energy ($\Delta G$) to estimate Ab–Ag interaction strength, (2) epitope SASA to measure differences in the solvent-accessible antigen surface area upon binding, and (3) complex structure confidence (AlphaFold pLDDT \cite{abramson2024accurate}) as a proxy for interface stability (Supplement \ref{sup:sec:computationalMetrics}).

