Figure \ref{fig:CA_density_plot} shows the density distribution of individual core ranges for the different years and seasons. Individual ranges differed significantly between years and seasons (ANOVA interaction between years and seasons, $F_{1,135}$=1.94, $p$=0.09; year: $p$<0.001; season: $p$ <0.001). During a given year, individual spider monkeys occupied larger core ranges during the dry season than during the wet season. This is particularly evident in 2014, 2015 and 2016.

