between sparsity -- measured as the $\ell_0$ norm of $\Z$, i.e., the number of non-zero entries per code vector -- and reconstruction quality, quantified by the $R^2$ score between the original activations $\A$ and their reconstructions $\Z\D$. This trade-off captures how well the learned codes retain information while encouraging interpretability through sparsity.
