For $\ell_2$-squared v/s kernel (solid) and modified $\ell_2$ vs kernel (dashed), kernel weights give an advantage by a factor of $\tilde{O}(d)$ and $\tilde{O}(\sqrt{d})$ respectively.
On the other hand, for modified $\ell_2$ v/s $\ell_2$-squared (long dashed), modified $\ell_2$ outperforms $\ell_2$-squared by a factor of $O(\sqrt{d})$.}
