\subsubsection{Average Connector Degree}
The average connector degree is the number of arcs entering or leaving a connector node divided by the total number of connectors~\cite[pp.120-121]{Men08}.
If this amount is high for a workflow net, it is less understandable than a workflow net with low average connector degree.
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:avg-conn-deg}
		\compavgconn(W) = 
			\frac{1}{|\mathcal{C}^W|} \cdot \sum_{x \in \mathcal{C}^W} \ndeg(x) 
\end{equation}
