\propitemf{\propfive}{\yes}
Let $M_1, \dots, M_n \in \mathcal{M}$ be workflow nets.
By definition, the depth of composed nets can be computed as follows:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\C(\parop(M_1, \dots, M_n)) = 1 + \max \{\C(M_1), \dots, \C(M_n)\}$,
\item $\C(\choiceop(M_1, \dots, M_n)) = 1 + \max \{\C(M_1), \dots, \C(M_n)\}$,
\item $\C(\loopop(M_1, \dots, M_n))$ \newline
$= \max \{\C(M_1), \C(M_2) + 1, \dots, \C(M_n) + 1\}$.
\end{itemize}
Therefore, $\C(\oplus(M_1, \dots, M_n)) \geq \C(M_i)$ for any $\oplus \in \{\parop, \choiceop, \loopop\}$ and $M_i \in \{M_1, \dots, M_n\}$.
Next, consider the sequential operator $\seqop$. 
Take the net $M = \seqop(M_1, \dots, M_n)$ and nodes $v_1, \dots, v_n$ such that $\min\{\lambda_{M_j}(v_j), \lambda_{\overleftarrow{M_j}}(v_j)\}$ for any $j \in \{1, \dots, n\}$, i.e. $v_j$ is the deepest node of the net $M_j$.
Then, we have $\lambda_M(v_j) \geq \lambda_{M_j}(v_j)$ and $\lambda_{\overleftarrow{M}}(v_j) \geq \lambda_{\overleftarrow{M_j}}(v_j)$.
We deduce:
\begin{eqnarray*}
\C(M)
&=& \max_{v}\{\min\{\lambda_{M}(v), \lambda_{\overleftarrow{M}}(v)\}\}\\
&=& \min\{\max\{\lambda_{M}(v_j) \mid 1 \leq j \leq n\}, \max\{\lambda_{\overleftarrow{M}}(v_j) \mid 1 \leq j \leq n\}\}\\
&\ge& \max\{\min\{\lambda_{M_j}(v_j), \lambda_{\overleftarrow{M_j}}(v_j) \mid 1 \leq j \leq n\}\}\\
&=& \max \{\C(M_1), \dots, \C(M_n)\}\\
&\ge& \C(M_i) \text{ for any } M_i \in \{M_1, \dots, M_n\}
\end{eqnarray*}
Therefore, $\C$ is monotone for all operations of Definition~\ref{def:operations}.

\propitemf{\propsix}{\no}
