\def\name{\diametername}
\def\C{\diameter}
\subsubsection{Diameter}
The diameter~\cite[p.119]{Men08} of a workflow net $W = (P,T,F,\ell,p_i,p_o)$ is the maximal length of a way from $p_i$ to $p_o$ where no arc is used more than once.
Note that, in contrast to paths, ways are allowed to revisit nodes.
The length of a way $w = v_1, \dots, v_k$ it the number of visited nodes, where revisited nodes can be counted more than once.
For $w = v_1, \dots, v_k$, we have $|w| = k$.
Let $\mathcal{W}_{p_i,p_o}$ be the set of all ways as defined above. 
We define:
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:diam}
\diameter(W) = \max\{|p| \mid p \in \mathcal{W}_{p_i, p_o}\}.
\end{equation}
