Let $M_1, M_2 \in \mathcal{M}$. 
For $i \in \{1,2\}$, let $f_i$ be the number of arcs in $M_i$, $t_i$ be the number of transitions in $M_i$ and $p_i$ be the number of places in $M_i$.
By arithmetic rules, we have: 
\begin{align*}
\C(M_1) + \C(M_2) &= \frac{f_1}{2t_1p_1 - 2t_1} + \frac{f_2}{2t_2p_2 - 2t_2} \\
&> \frac{f_1 + f_2}{2t_1p_1 - 2t_1 + 2t_2p_2 - 2t_2} =: \frac{n}{d}
\end{align*}
\begin{itemize}
\item The operator $\seqop$ introduces $1$ transition and $2$ arcs.
