\subsubsection{Number of Empty Sequence Flows}
The measure for empty sequence flows is based on work of Gruhn et al.~\cite{GruL09} on reducing the complexity of BPMN.
They found that, in BPMN models, there are often edes that directly connect and-splits and -joins. 
These edges can be removed completely, as they don't change the behavior of the net.
Regarding workflow nets, there can't be any edges between two and-connectors, since and-connectors are always transitions and Petri nets are bipartite.
Instead, empty sequence flows in workflow nets are places that have only and-splits in their preset and and-joins in their postset. 
We therefore define:
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:empty}
\C(W) = |\{p \in P \mid \pre{p} \subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\text{and}}^W \land \post{p} \subseteq \mathcal{J}_{\text{and}}^W\}|
\end{equation}
